E. Proof-facing synthesis
  The strict HYP-3437 overlap core is the safe theorem object.  The incident
  core is a router: it collapses all 59 negative rows to size at most 2, but
  it forgets which co-owners make a touched atom taxable.  The missing lemma
  is therefore not a scalar bound; it is a transfer theorem from touched
  overlap atoms to strict subset tax, or to HYP-3436 survivor-gate words.
  The C3 skeleton says most hard rows use binding-unit pairs; Qsqrt_minus7
  separates the two quadratic characters inside each binding pair.  The two
  ramified-apex rows are the explicit apex-7 covering-layer exceptions.
  The 12->24 hinge remains a 2-adic boundary exit, not a 7-adic census proof.

F. Special-function guardrails
  Euler-Mascheroni and Meissel-Mertens data are legal only as reciprocal
  endpoint-budget priorities.  Ramanujan-Soldner is a balance-root metaphor
  for locating a finite transition, not a certificate.  Sophie Germain
  factorization belongs to quartic height-wall splits.  Krasner protects
  local p-adic branch stability.  Hermite-Lindemann-Weierstrass is only a
  no-free-slider guard: a transcendence slogan cannot replace endpoint
  owners, wall labels, or strict overlap atoms.

