H. Assumption challenge
  Considered vertices: runners, odd blockers, even-half gates, fixed
  circle sections, section boundaries, wall crossings, residues, cover arcs,
  Fourier modes, matroid circuits, strict overlap subsets, incident tax
  owners, endpoint labels, survivor-gate words, and proof obligations.
  Chosen quotient: incident tax owners plus endpoint/survivor bridge tests.
  It preserves the one-branch deficit/tax comparison as an inequality target
  but destroys internal co-owner multiplicity.  Challenged assumption: the
  HYP-3437 rank-6 AP core must be attacked as six independent runners; the
  incident quotient says it is mostly a two-owner residue/endpoint bridge.
